# Dev processes already running

Before `.\scripts\run-server.ps1`, `.\scripts\run-client.ps1`, or `.\scripts\run-dashboard.ps1`:

1. Read the metadata of every terminal already open in this Cursor window (pid, cwd, active command, last exit code). Check all of them, not only the terminal that is focused.
2. If that script is already the active command, do not open another terminal and do not run it again. Use the existing one.
3. If no terminal shows it, check the listening port: API **8080**, clinic **1420**, dashboard **1421**. A listener means it is already up. Stop. Do not start a second copy.

Do not `Stop-Process`, free those ports, or replace a running dev process unless the user explicitly asked to restart that process.

A health check is only a check. "Address already in use," a failed bind, or a background-terminal notification after the reply is sent means leave the existing process alone. Do not start the script again.
